ial capital of 250  seven engineers set up the business  marking the beginning of the private  tech industry in india  today it's one of the biggest companies  in the world with a market  capitalization of over 95 billion  dollars  infosys in some sense is india's  original startup when infosys  began in 1981 it was in a socialistic  era when india was not really that  friendly towards business and we had  many many challenges for example just  getting a telephone connection would  take two years  to import even a single computer you  have to go to delhi to get a license  and even if you had to make a small  change  in the configuration of the computer  that you purchased you have to go back  and get the license changed all over  again  then came economic liberalization in the  1990s  the government deregulated markets and  reduced taxes and import tariffs  emphasis and other it companies thrived  in 1993 emphasis went public and built  india's first software campus in  bangalore  prompted by this technology boom in the  1990s people from all over india poured  into bangalore to work or study  so bangalore was the takeoff point for a  lot of those people that came to study  and then went overseas to study further  to get postgraduate degrees or work in a  lot of these global companies perhaps  most of them in the united states and  they've made a comfortable life for  themselves overseas and never returned  but something changed in the late 1990s  and 2000s bangalore became a valid  destination to chase a career in  technology on its own  many local talents especially those from  humble roots decided to stay  lots of overseas indians returned to  bangalore as well vani cola was one of  them she built and sold two startups in  silicon valley before starting a venture  capital firm in bangalore in 2006.  i was in india end of 2005  for a long trip which i hadn't done  in the two decades that i was gone and  for me it was just a very different  country to the one i lef