 smartphones as a  medium to reach out  [Music]  2021 has been a breakout year for these  startups during the covert 19 pandemic  many consumers have turned to online  services for grocery deliveries tutoring  and medical diagnosis contributing to  surging revenues billions of dollars  have poured into india in july for  instance as in china the communist party  has cracked down on a lot of these  technology companies indian startups  gathered almost 8 billion dollars in  venture and pe capital making india for  the very first time overtake china as a  venture capital destination  record numbers of unicorns have been  born at an unprecedented speed  and investors are hoping to profit from  companies that could become the next  google or facebook global investors  always asked  where is the exit and in startup lingo  that means  how do i  make a return on my investment suddenly  a lot of these startups have plans to  debut in the public markets and now that  is a legit exit and investors then  triple four times 10 times their  investments  that is what's happened this year with  the public market debut of a food  delivery startup called zamato which was  really the game changer i think thrice  at our in our journey we've gotten to a  point that  we can't do this anymore right and this  just cannot be done  but um  we actually like continue for one more  day and it's and it all gets over and it  all starts again  zomato as a company is neither  profitable and its medium term prospects  for profitability are really mediocre  but retail investors have lapped up the  shares of zamato sending the valuation  of the company soaring to 13 billion on  debut  but digital payment firm paytm's ipo in  november which is india's biggest ever  has been a disappointment  it raised 2.5 billion dollars but the  stock price has sunk dramatically making  it one of the worst initial showings by  a major tech firm since the dot-com  bubble era of the late 1990s  like zamato paytm is not p