gh to start a  company in india as you scale i think  you run into a lot of areas where  regulation is not clear one thing would  be industry by industry for  government and government bodies to  continue to work to be a step ahead in  terms of providing clear regulatory  guidelines and continuing to engage  industry in modifying that  but starting up in india still has  advantages  half of the indian population is under  the age of 25.  young indians adapt to technology easily  and could be potential consumers with  spending power in the long term they  also provide the country with a rich  talent pool  india has about  four and a half million software  engineers and within the next 10 years  this is going to double  so as the technology talent improves in  the country it will provide a fertile  ground to create more startups it's a  still a nascent ecosystem just about at  takeoff point but a lot of entrepreneurs  are actually dreaming big  entrepreneurship is uh it's it's not a  skill it's a mindset it's a mindset  where you don't take no for an answer  if you are passionate about what you are  doing and if that is making an impact  like i'm sure that we can do this for  decades  you

